{"args":{"resource":"reference/methodology_summary.md"},"client_id":"CL-B","entry_hash":"669333c1d1897288c245d4263ce922c03d2e2124f888c78783feebe55438101d","prev_hash":"9afb23f7973ed129f6492c8908d692d1e950e902a0b23e2f10d97a22c7324940","response":{"classification":"CLIENT-LICENSED","data":"# Methodology summary (client-visible)\n\n**Apparel Purchase Intent Survey.** A monthly online survey of about 3,000 U.S. adults, weighted to Census benchmarks. The headline measure, `intent_pct`, is the percent of adults planning to buy apparel in the next 30 days. Margins of error (`moe95_pts`) are 95% intervals that include a design effect for weighting. At the national level they are about ±2 points; for regions they are about ±3–5 points.\n\n**Spending Momentum Index (SMI).** A proprietary Halvorsen composite of survey intent and transaction-data signals, indexed to 100. The construction and weights are proprietary.\n\n**HX-APP forecast.** Halvorsen's proprietary model of U.S. apparel retail sales, year over year. The published outputs are point forecasts with 80% prediction intervals. Driver attributions show how much each input moved the forecast in the model. They are model attributions, not measured causal effects.\n\n**Brand trackers (custom).** Client-commissioned studies of brand consideration. Results belong to the commissioning client.\n","licensed_to":["CL-A","CL-B"],"resource":"reference/methodology_summary.md"},"response_sha256":"1e692ada1e2bfc80444df475fe5f15132bede704d14e23d1ca6b88cb1e5fae89","seq":2,"tool":"read_resource","ts_utc":"2026-09-30T20:32:58Z"}
{"args":{"resource":"reference/market_events.md"},"client_id":"CL-B","entry_hash":"80923a8726a2d5f3edfb3b0951a8f019f78865d5762a054e2abdbc9bcbcdf494","prev_hash":"669333c1d1897288c245d4263ce922c03d2e2124f888c78783feebe55438101d","response":{"classification":"CLIENT-LICENSED","data":"# Market events digest (client-visible; compiled by Halvorsen from public sources)\n\n- **2026-03** Regular gasoline prices rose for a third straight month (public EIA data).\n- **2026-04 to 2026-06** Several apparel chains, including Crestline, opened new stores across the South (trade press).\n- **2026-06** Northgate Outfitters launched \"Northgate Rewards\", a national loyalty program (company press release, June 2).\n- **2026-07** Back-to-school promotions started earlier than usual at several national retailers (trade press).\n- **2026-08** Consumer confidence proxies ticked up (public survey releases).\n","licensed_to":["CL-A","CL-B"],"resource":"reference/market_events.md"},"response_sha256":"8b63fc4c85b272f9ad362c1094726d7d158c41e8e024176199949ed2543970e9","seq":3,"tool":"read_resource","ts_utc":"2026-09-30T20:32:58Z"}
